    {
      "id": "790b6b76-c762-4779-b538-cff59372d7d7",
      "name": "Template overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 540,
        "height": 1240,
        "content": "## Draft Gmail replies to stock and visit inquiries with Claude\n\n### Who's it for\nSmall shops that answer customer emails about stock and store visits, and want replies drafted by AI but sent by a person.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every 5 minutes, gets up to 10 new emails sent to your inquiry address that have no label yet.\n2. Claude sorts each email into stock inquiry, store visit, or other.\n3. Stock inquiries: Claude extracts the product type, the workflow looks it up in the `products` Data Table, and Claude writes a reply based only on the results.\n4. Store visits: Claude extracts the date (today's date is passed in, so \"this Saturday\" works), and the reply suggests open slots from the `visit_slots` Data Table.\n5. The reply is saved as a Gmail draft in the same thread, and the email gets the `ai-drafted` label. Other emails get the `needs-human` label. **Nothing is sent.**\n\n### How to set up\n1. Add Anthropic and Gmail credentials.\n2. Create two Data Tables and select them in the two lookup nodes:\n   - `products`: sku, name, category, color, width_cm, price, stock, note\n   - `visit_slots`: slot_date (YYYY-MM-DD), slot_time, capacity, booked\n3. Create the Gmail labels `ai-drafted` and `needs-human`, and select them in the two label nodes.\n4. Edit the **Config** node: inbox address, signature, timezone, currency.\n5. Run it once, read the drafts, then publish.\n\n### Requirements\nGmail account and Anthropic API key.\n\n### How to customize\nChange the product categories in **Extract product category**, and the reply rules in the two reply nodes. AI drafts can still contain promises that are not in your data, so read each draft before you send it.\n\nA write-up of how this template was built and tested, with screenshots (in Japanese): https://outsidernotes.com/n8n-template-gmail-stock-visit-drafts/"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "237de9fb-2384-4603-8d8a-df3101e03d7f",
      "name": "Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -50,
        90
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 868,
        "height": 524,
        "content": "## 1. Get new emails\nRuns every 5 minutes and loops over unlabeled emails sent to the inquiry address in **Config**."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9b90ef96-5ade-4a59-922e-682831b8a71c",
      "name": "Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        842,
        -58
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1352,
        "height": 828,
        "content": "## 2. Classify, look up, and write\nClaude sorts the email, extracts the product type or visit date, looks it up in the Data Tables, and writes a reply based only on the results. Other emails go straight to the **needs-human** label."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "09792595-2063-4830-8245-e6b8b060c83a",
      "name": "Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2346,
        -58
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 424,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## 3. Save as a draft and label\nThe reply is saved as a draft in the same Gmail thread. Labels keep each email from being processed twice. Nothing is sent automatically."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
